# E2E conventions

Stack: Playwright + playwright-bdd + TypeScript. Generated `.features-gen/` is never edited by hand (`pnpm bddgen`).

## Source of truth

| What | Where | Owner |
|------|-------|-------|
| Test cases (Steps / Expected) | `docs/testcases/*.csv` (UTF-8 export of the Excel sheet) | Tester |
| Automation status per TC | CSV column `Automation` | Tester + engineer |
| Spec / tester checklist | `docs/specs/{domain}/{FLOW}.md`, `docs/scenario/{domain}/{FLOW}_TESTER_VERIFY.md` | Generated by `/tc-spec`, reviewed by tester |
| Case rows | `features/{domain}/datasets/*.dataset.ts` | Tester (existing flows) / engineer (new flows) |
| UI logic | `features/{domain}/pages/*Page.ts` | Engineer |

Expected comes **only** from the CSV. Blank Expected → `Out`, never invented. CSV vs code/docs mismatch → `Conflict`, never silently resolved.

## Excel / CSV columns

Original columns stay as they are: `No, Title, Pre-condition, Steps, Expected results, Results, Test Date, Executed by, Note`. Added columns (read by name, not position):

| Column | Required | Values |
|--------|----------|--------|
| `caseId` | when `Auto` | camelCase intent id(s), comma-separated if one TC maps to several |
| `Automation` | yes once triaged | `Auto` / `Manual` / `Out` / `Open` / `Conflict` |
| `Domain` | when `Auto` | path under `features/`, e.g. `authentication`, `mail/advanced-search` |
| `Flow` | optional | one value of the dataset `flow` union |
| `Tag` | optional | `@skip-ci`, `@mode:serial`, … |

Section header rows (e.g. `Login`) and continuation rows (empty Title) are kept as-is.

## Repo layout

```text
features/{domain}/
  datasets/{flow}.dataset.ts     # export DATASET + get{Xxx}Case
  pages/{Flow}Page.ts            # runCase / expectCase
  fixtures.ts                    # test = shared test + this domain's POM fixtures
  tests/{nn}_{flow}.feature      # Scenario Outline + Examples
  tests/steps.ts                 # exactly the runner steps, nothing else
shared/
  env.ts                         # requireEnv, AUTH_FILE (env only, no fallbacks for secrets)
  fixtures.ts                    # base test; @unauthenticated → empty storageState
  steps/common.steps.ts          # `Given the user is signed in` (the only sign-in step)
scripts/check-testcase-sync.ts   # pnpm check:sync (check-only)
```

New shared helpers (seed, retry, …) go to `shared/` only when a second domain needs them.

## Dataset contract

```ts
export type XxxCaseId = "caseA" | "caseB";

export type XxxCase = {
  id: XxxCaseId;
  tc: readonly string[];          // CSV TC ids, [] only for harness cases not in CSV
  note: string;                   // "TC_12: short intent" — shown in report titles
  flow: "flowA" | "flowB";        // branches inside runCase
  expect: { /* only flags confirmed by CSV Expected */ };
};

export const DATASET = { /* keyed by caseId */ } as const satisfies Record<XxxCaseId, XxxCase>;

export function getXxxCase(caseId: string): XxxCase { /* throw listing known ids */ }
```

`pnpm check:sync` imports every `*.dataset.ts` and reads `DATASET`.

## Feature shape

```gherkin
Feature: {Title}
  Spec: docs/specs/{domain}/{FLOW}.md
  Tester verify: docs/scenario/{domain}/{FLOW}_TESTER_VERIFY.md
  Dataset: features/{domain}/datasets/{flow}.dataset.ts
  Out of scope: TC_… (Manual / Out / Open / Conflict)
  Mode: BDD+DDT

  @{domain} @authenticated
  Scenario Outline: {Flow} case from dataset
    Given the user is signed in
    When the user runs {flow label} case "<caseId>"
    Then the {flow label} case "<caseId>" should pass

    Examples: [<caseId>] <note>
      | caseId | note                 |
      | caseA  | TC_12: short intent  |
```

- Anonymous Outline: tag `@unauthenticated`, no `Given the user is signed in`.
- Plain Scenario only for a one-off flow that cannot share the runner steps.
- Tags: `@{domain}`, `@authenticated` / `@unauthenticated`, `@skip-ci` (add a comment with the reason), `@mode:serial`.

## Steps and POM

- `tests/steps.ts` holds only the two runner steps, created with `createBdd(test)` from the domain `fixtures.ts`.
- POM is injected as a fixture (no `new Page()` in steps, no module-level state).
- `runCase(caseId)` switches on `row.flow`; `expectCase(caseId)` asserts each `row.expect` flag that is set.
- Navigation uses relative paths (`page.goto("/mail")`, baseURL comes from `BASE_URL`).

## Banned (enforced by `pnpm check:sync`)

- `page.waitForTimeout(…)` without an `// allow-wait: <reason>` comment on the same line.
- Fallback assertions that always pass, e.g. `.or(page.locator("main"))`.
- Secrets in code, features or docs. Credentials live in `.env` (gitignored); `playwright/.auth/` is gitignored.
- Random choices without logging the picked value.

## Verify before a PR

```bash
pnpm verify          # typecheck + bddgen + check:sync
pnpm test            # or: pnpm exec playwright test features/{domain}
```

Session for `@authenticated`: `pnpm auth:login` (re-run when it expires).
